.Dd June 10, 2026
.Dt ZDOTS-PATCH-EXPORT 1
.Os zdots
.Sh NAME
.Nm zdots-patch-export
.Nd export git patches to a timestamped outbox for transfer
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Ar target
.Op Ar ref
.Op Fl -name Ar slug
.Op Fl -outbox Ar dir
.Op Fl - Ar git-diff-args ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
produces a single
.Pa .patch
file from a git repository and writes it to an outbox directory
.Pq default: Pa ~/Desktop/outbox
with a timestamp-prefixed, descriptive filename.
It is designed for the personal dots and config workflow: generate a patch
on one machine, transfer it, apply it on another.
.Pp
Two patch strategies are selected automatically based on whether a
.Ar ref
is supplied:
.Bl -tag -width uncommitted
.It Em Uncommitted Pq default
.Xr git-diff 1
.Li HEAD
captures all staged and unstaged changes relative to HEAD in a single
unified diff.
Apply on the receiving end with:
.Dl git apply <patch>
Use this for work-in-progress that has not yet been committed.
.It Em Ref or range
.Xr git-format-patch 1
embeds the commit message, author, and date in a mail-formatted patch.
Apply on the receiving end with:
.Dl git am <patch>
Use this for shipping a finished, committed change.
.El
.Pp
If there is nothing to export
.Pq clean working tree or empty format-patch output ,
.Nm
prints
.Dq no patch to create
and exits 0.
.Pp
The outbox directory is created automatically if it does not exist.
Patch files are named
.Sm off
.Ar YYYYMMDDTHHMMSS - slug - descriptor .patch
.Sm on
so that
.Xr ls 1
lists them in chronological order.
.Sh TARGETS
A target selects the repository to patch.
If omitted the current working directory is used.
.Bl -tag -width production
.It Ic zdots
.Pa ~/.config/zsh
.It Ic adots
.Pa $HOME
tracked via the bare repository at
.Pa ~/.homegit .
.It Ic vdots
.Pa ~/.config/nvim
.It Ar path
Any directory inside a git repository.
The patch name slug is derived from the
.Li origin
remote URL, falling back to the directory basename.
.El
.Sh REF
An optional ref selects which commits to include.
When omitted, uncommitted changes are exported.
.Bl -tag -width Ar
.It Ar sha
Single commit.
Passed to
.Xr git-format-patch 1
as
.Fl 1 Ar sha .
.It Ar from Ns Li .. Ns Ar to
Commit range.
Passed to
.Xr git-format-patch 1
directly.
.It Ar branch
Tip of a branch.
Passed to
.Xr git-format-patch 1
as
.Fl 1 Ar branch .
.El
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Fl
.It Fl -name Ar slug
Override the descriptive slug embedded in the patch filename.
Useful when the remote URL would produce a poor name.
.It Fl -outbox Ar dir
Write the patch to
.Ar dir
instead of the default outbox.
Created automatically if absent.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Show usage.
.It Fl -
Pass remaining arguments to
.Xr git-diff 1
.Pq uncommitted mode only .
Use
.Fl -stat
to preview the diff without producing a patch file.
.El
.Sh OUTBOX NAMING
Patch files follow the pattern:
.Pp
.Dl YYYYMMDDTHHMMSS-{slug}-{descriptor}.patch
.Pp
.Bl -tag -width descriptor -compact
.It Em slug
Derived from the remote origin URL, the known label
.Pq Li zdots , Li adots , Li vdots ,
or
.Fl -name .
.It Em descriptor
.Li uncommitted
for the diff-HEAD path; the shortened SHA or branch name for the
format-patch path; a
.Li from_to
pair for a range.
.El
.Sh PATCH STRATEGY GUIDANCE
For a personal workflow without kernel-style review overhead:
.Bl -bullet
.It
Use the uncommitted default for WIP changes that have not been committed.
Apply with
.Xr git-apply 1 .
.It
Commit your work first and pass a
.Ar ref
when you want the commit message and authorship preserved in the patch.
Apply with
.Xr git-am 1 .
.It
.Nm
prints the correct apply command after writing each patch.
A header comment inside each file also records the apply command.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width ZDOTS_PATCH_OUTBOX
.It Ev ZDOTS_PATCH_OUTBOX
Override the outbox directory globally.
Set in the adots shell environment to redirect patches on all machines
without a per-call flag.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Pa
.It Pa ~/Desktop/outbox/
Default outbox directory.
Created on first use.
.It Pa ~/Desktop/outbox/ Ns Ar timestamp Ns - Ns Ar slug Ns - Ns Ar descriptor Ns Pa .patch
Individual patch file.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Sh EXAMPLES
Export uncommitted zdots changes:
.Pp
.Dl zdots-patch-export zdots
.Pp
Export uncommitted adots changes:
.Pp
.Dl zdots-patch-export adots
.Pp
Export the last committed zdots change as a format-patch:
.Pp
.Dl zdots-patch-export zdots HEAD~1
.Pp
Export a specific commit from vdots:
.Pp
.Dl zdots-patch-export vdots abc1234
.Pp
Export a commit range:
.Pp
.Dl zdots-patch-export zdots HEAD~3..HEAD
.Pp
Export uncommitted changes from an arbitrary repo with a custom name:
.Pp
.Dl zdots-patch-export ~/work/myrepo --name myfix
.Pp
Preview what the uncommitted diff contains without writing a file:
.Pp
.Dl zdots-patch-export zdots -- --stat
.Pp
Apply an uncommitted-mode patch on the receiving machine:
.Pp
.Dl git apply 20260610T120000-zdots-uncommitted.patch
.Pp
Apply a format-patch on the receiving machine:
.Pp
.Dl git am 20260610T120000-zdots-HEAD~1.patch
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr zdots-server-keys 1 ,
.Xr zdots-github-keys 1 ,
.Xr git-diff 1 ,
.Xr git-format-patch 1 ,
.Xr git-apply 1 ,
.Xr git-am 1 ,
.Xr zdots 7
